FROM ZERO TO main()  —  BOOTLOADER FUNDAMENTALS
Cortex-M  |  flash layout from the referenced guide

MEMORY MAP (example)
0x00000000  bootrom     bootloader image
0x00004000  approm      application image
0x00030000  flash end   (board-dependent)

KEY REGIONS
bootrom   read-only flash holding reset + jump logic
approm    application .text / vectors
eram      optional RAM copy of app (relocated firmware)
shared    RAM used for reboot counter / handshake

LINKER SYMBOLS (typical)
__bootrom_start__
__bootrom_end__
__approm_start__
__approm_end__
__eram_start__          /* load address != run address when using AT> */

CORE TYPES / REGISTERS
uint32_t *vtor          Vector Table Offset Register (SCB->VTOR)
uint32_t  msp           Main Stack Pointer (loaded from vector[0])
void    (*reset)(void)  Reset handler (vector[1], jumped with BX)
uint32_t  boot_count    persistent counter in shared RAM (no-init)

BOOT SEQUENCE (minimal)
1. CPU reset  ->  SP = *(uint32_t*)bootrom
2. PC = reset handler in bootrom
3. optional: check app valid / reboot loop
4. SCB->VTOR = (uint32_t)__approm_start__   /* 256-byte aligned */
5. __set_MSP(*(uint32_t*)__approm_start__)
6. jump:  ((void(*)(void))*(uint32_t*)(__approm_start__+4))()

ADVANCED KNOBS
MPU region over bootrom     lock bootloader against app writes
memcpy(eram, approm, size)  run app from RAM
objcopy --pad-to --gap-fill 0xFF   then cat boot.bin app.bin

PREREQ
linker scripts, Cortex-M startup, VTOR, ARM bx/msr, sector alignment
